{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/781049-how-do-you-make-your-characters-your-own","id":781049,"title":"How do you make your characters your own?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-06T02:58:34-08:00","id":781049,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> How do you make your characters your own?","content":"I got to thinking about this at first for video games/MMOs... in Final Fantasy XIV, I carefully think over how I want my character to look. I don't change it super often (for my main class) and try to make sure I choose those things which all speak to her personality. It gets weirder/amusing when you consider that this character is based off a character I played in a 13th Age game and when a friend from that game also started on FF XIV... in the table top our characters were romantically linked, eventually married, and we even got dice boxes and towers with their shared &quot;symbol&quot; because they were the best... around... anyways, so of course in Final Fantasy they HAD to get the Eternal Bond ceremony... because we're super geeky.<br /> <br /> But, I'm getting slightly off my own topic here, which is that I take a lot of time to add and pick things that speak to the character as I see them. And when I consider the character I mentioned above in her table top incarnation it makes me realize I do that with those characters too. I choose pictures that I find representative, I commission art, I make playlists of music that speaks to them (side note: beware the characters with end of game boss music as part of their playlist...).<br /> <br /> So I pose to you, how do you (and if you're willing to provide examples, feel free!) do this with your own characters? Video games, table top, anything where you have had a character you've done something along these lines for... anything goes!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T10:21:20-08:00","id":781190,"title":"","content":"Here's what I do: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Think of concepts</li> <li>Pick best concept for game</li> <li>Think of backstory</li> <li>Make sheet</li> <li>Realize I don't have enough points to make what I planned</li> <li>Revise character backstory</li> <li>Realize that someone else in the group made a similar character and revise my character further</li> <li>Realize the character is no longer my original plan and revise backstory to fit character's final revision</li> <li>???</li> <li>Profit</li> </ol><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T11:51:55-08:00","id":781224,"title":"","content":"Well, I don't have great experience with how a character might develop over time and how that affects things, but one thing I tend to do at character creation is to define a character's &quot;trick&quot;. One or a few things that will be central to the idea of that character. This could be a character quality, such as being shy or aggressive, but I'd rather it was an action or a method since that's more flexible. It could be something they're really good at, but they don't <i>have</i> to be: it could also be something they aspire to be good at, or don't have any personal realation to it at all but just tends to do anyway.<br /> <br /> What type of things are fit for this? Well, it's hard to describe, but... imagine Street Fighter IV, right? Think about Ryu. I'd say his &quot;tricks&quot; are shoryuken and hadouken. It's not the light jabs, but not the ultimates either. It's something you can use regularly, but not something so basic you can't <i>not</i> do it as well. It's something that's really neat when it works, but not something that would cost your character their credibility if it whiffs, either. When it's something that your character can choose to do, and often does, then it's a &quot;trick&quot;. And if I know them, I can often calculate the rest of my character from there (which doesn't mean that no other things matter to the character, of course, but that's how I'd say I make my character <i>mine</i>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}